cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Lanternlight
message: >-
  If you use Lanternlight, or cite a number measured by it, please cite the
  release you actually read. Every figure this project publishes is tied to a
  specific game build, and a build that has been patched is a different
  measurement.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Moonbeam
repository-code: https://github.com/Remus3/Lanternlight
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-06'
abstract: >-
  A companion and analysis project for the extraction ARPG Mistfall Hunter
  (Steam appid 3282300) that never touches the game process. The game ships
  kernel-level anti-cheat, so Lanternlight injects nothing, reads no process
  memory, captures no network traffic and hooks no swapchain. It derives
  everything from files the game itself writes into user-writable space - a
  live-appending log, plain GVAS save files and a market price cache - plus
  passive capture of the operator's own screen.

  Its purpose is measurement. No cooldowns, damage coefficients or stealth
  durations have been published for this game, and the fan sites that quote
  such numbers cross-copy each other rather than measuring. Lanternlight's
  Emberforge engine is built on the opposite rule: omit rather than guess, keep
  an unmeasured value distinguishable from a measured zero, and record how each
  observation was established at the moment it is made.

  Not affiliated with Bellring Games, Skystone Games or Valve.
keywords:
  - mistfall-hunter
  - game-companion
  - anti-cheat-safe
  - unreal-engine
  - gvas
  - log-parsing
  - theorycrafting
  - measurement
